{
  "_about": "Phase D-2b scenario metadata.  The d2b-twelve-scenarios.sh bash script\n  reads this file INSTEAD of inferring verdict expectations from baked-in branches\n  inside the script.  Two reasons:\n  (a) chart-policy-driven CLOSED verdicts are graded CHART_INTENTIONAL_DENY\n      so PASS_OK math is well-defined and chart-policy regressions are loud\n      (they flip CHART_INTENTIONAL_DENY to DENY_LEAK);\n  (b) fixture label selectors, namespaces, etc. are pulled from this single\n      file so CNI tests and fixture YAMLs cannot drift.\n\n  Each entry has:\n    id:            stable scenario id used in the run record\n    description:   human-readable summary\n    role:          gateway | worker | ingress-controller | prometheus | untrusted\n    action:        what the source pod does (http_get, tcp_connect, dns_lookup)\n    target_kind:   service | pod | external_ip\n    target_svc:    ClusterIP service name (if target_kind=service)\n    target_pod_selector: selector pinning the target pod if target_kind != service\n    target_pod_name_or_typed_localhost: when \"local\" means the source must target\n                       its own pod (cni-arbitrary fixture) via Pod IP\n    target_host:   hostname or IP the source connects to\n    target_port:   int\n    expected:      ALLOW | DENY\n    chart_intent:  ALLOW_IMPLIED | ALLOW_FEATURE_OFF | DENY_DEFAULT_DENY | DENY_DIRECT_EGRESS\n                    | DENY_PORT_MISUSE | DENY_EXTERNAL_IP | DENY_METADATA | DENY_OPEN_INTENT\n    upstream_reason:        short text used for hints when regressed\n    requires_features:      list<name> — keys in values.yaml that must be true\n    ignores_l1:   bool — true when the target has no localhost listener by definition\n    ignores_l2:   bool — true when the host is a raw IP / not a service hostname\n",
